    "synthesis_verdict": "Q_R(q) = \u03a3_\u03bb dim_q(V_\u03bb)\u00b7mult_R(\u03bb) defines the q-deformed icosahedral character matrix's row sums; for A_5 the H-sector Q_H(q) = 2\u00b7[5]_q has closed-form h-expansion 10 + 10h\u00b2 + 2h\u2074 (by algebraic identity [5]_q = h\u2074+5h\u00b2+5). The structural h\u2074 coefficient is +2 \u2014 DIFFERENT in sign AND magnitude from the Borromean H_3 reference h\u2074 = \u22123/4. This complements T5: the H-sector carries its own h\u2074 structure, but in a different group algebra than the Borromean trace coefficient \u2014 the ratio +2/(\u22123/4) = \u22128/3 has no clean structural meaning. The Clifford excess identity \u03a3_R Q_R \u2212 \u03a3_\u03bb dim_q = dim_q(\u03bb_self-conj) holds to machine precision for both A_4 (excess = dim_q((2,2))) and A_5 (excess = dim_q((3,1,1))) \u2014 this is the Wedderburn decomposition's q-deformed signature: self-conjugate partitions split into 2 conjugate A_n irreps under Res^{S_n}_{A_n}, and the excess weighting tracks this splitting at q \u2260 1. The q-deformed icosahedral matrix is a well-defined object at q_0; its H-sector's h\u2074 structure is internally clean but NOT linked to the 3-strand h\u2074 obstruction."
